#decision("Original generic circuits instead of commercial schematics")[
*Options:* model a commercial product from its service manual, or design original circuits with the same topologies. *Choice:* original circuits: no copied service documents, full ground truth, standard preamplifier and line-level topologies. *Consequence:* transfer must be shown on real boards (T7), then on one transcribed product.
]

<< part(3, "Objectives and measurable success criteria") >>

<% set short = {'T2': "channel strip", 'T3': "in the top three", 'T8': "effort ÷ chart's", 'T10': "÷ random's", 'T11': "complaint read ÷ ignored", 'T14': "wrong prior", 'T22': "out-of-catalog", 'T23': "single faults", 'T24': "powered readings above 50 V ÷ half-split's", 'T18': "complaint-reading F1", 'T19': "meter photos exact", 'T20': "p95 time per step", 'T21': "API cost per diagnosis"} %>
<% set secs = [] %><% for o in ['O1', 'O2', 'O3', 'O4', 'O5'] %><% set items = [] %><% for s in targets.targets if s.role == 'secondary' and s.objective == o %><% set _ = items.append(s.id ~ " " ~ short[s.id] ~ " " ~ s.text | replace("; ", " and ")) %><% endfor %><% if items %><% set _ = secs.append("(" ~ o ~ ") " ~ items | join(", ")) %><% endif %><% endfor %>
*Objectives.* (O1) Name the group (faults whose readings match within tolerance at every test point) containing the failed part, on as-new and aged units; (O2) with less effort to a confirmed answer than scripted troubleshooting; (O3) with its uncertainty shown: calibrated probabilities, ambiguity groups, an explicit "no single fault fits"; (O4) safely: no unsafe step or invented reading; (O5) practically: fast, cheap, reading plain complaints and meter photos. @tab:targets lists the primaries and release gates; the secondary targets, reported but not deciding success, are << secs | join("; ") | esc >> (Claude parts need an API key).

*Effort.* A DC reading costs << num(m('library.design.cost_dc'), 0) >> unit, an oscilloscope reading << num(m('library.design.cost_scope'), 0) >>, a point that can exceed 50 V << num(m('library.design.cost_hv_extra'), 0) >> more (leads clipped on with the power off) and unsoldering a part << num(m('library.design.cost_lift'), 0) >>, within a budget of << num(m('library.design.budget'), 0) >>. Every method is charged one unsoldering test to confirm its named suspect unless it already confirmed one. Every comparison is repeated with the scope, unsoldering and high-voltage weights halved and doubled, and effort becomes bench minutes once the tickets and S1 give step times.

